    "title": "Why I Started Running",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Two years ago, I was not fit. I drove everywhere, I ate a lot of fast food, and I never did any sport. When I climbed the stairs at work, I was out of breath after only one floor. One day my doctor told me, 'You must do more exercise.' I did not like this idea, but I knew she was right."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "I decided to start running because it was cheap. I only needed a pair of shoes. At first, it was very difficult. I could run for only two minutes, and then I had to walk. My legs hurt for days. A colleague, Nina, told me to be patient and to run three times a week, so I made a plan and followed it."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "After a month, I could run for twenty minutes without stopping. I felt stronger, and I slept better at night. After six months, I entered a small race of five kilometres in my town. I finished in thirty-eight minutes, and I was very proud, even though I came near the end."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Now I run four times a week, usually in the morning before work. I have lost eight kilos, and I eat more vegetables. I also joined a running club, where I made new friends. My advice to beginners is simple: start slowly, find a friend to run with, and never give up. It gets easier!"
      }
    ]
  },
